Hands-On Jenkins Declarative Pipeline Assignments for DevOps Learners

If you’re learning Jenkins CI/CD and want to move beyond theory, here are real-world Jenkins Declarative Pipeline assignments for practice:

🧩 Assignment 1 – Pipeline Basics
 ✔ Create a declarative pipeline
 ✔ Print system info (hostname, OS, user)
 ✔ Understand stages & steps

🧩 Assignment 2 – Git + Build
 ✔ Checkout code from GitHub
 ✔ Run build command (npm / maven)
 ✔ Use post { success / failure }

🧩 Assignment 3 – Docker Build & Environment Variables
 ✔ Build Docker image from Dockerfile
 ✔ Use image name via variables

🧩 Assignment 4 – Secure Credentials 🔐
 ✔ Push Docker image to Docker Hub
 ✔ Use Jenkins Credentials Store
 ✔ No plain-text secrets

🧩 Assignment 5 – Deployment
 ✔ Stop & remove old container
 ✔ Deploy new container using Docker

🧩 Assignment 6 – Conditional Deployment
 ✔ Deploy only when branch = main

🧩 Assignment 7 – Full CI/CD Pipeline
 ✔ Git → Test → Build → Push → Deploy
 ✔ Add post actions

🎯 Goal: Write the Jenkinsfile for each assignment and test it in a real Jenkins environment (Docker / EC2).
